GtA UNIVERSITY MATHURAEND TERIT{ EXAMINATION, ?OLL.IzCOURSE: . B.TECH II-YEAR, III-SEMSUBIECT: DISCRETE MATHEMATICS [CSE213) UNI. ROIL No:TIME:ZHRS 30 MIN MAXMARKS:80Note:-1. Answer all questions from Group A, Any Four from Group B and Any Four from Group C.2. All parts of a question (a, b, etc.) should be answered at one place.3. Answer should be brief and to-the-point and be supplemented with neat sketches.4. Any missing or wrong data may be assumed suitably giving proper justification.5. Figures on the right-hand side margin indicate full marks.GROUP AQ1. Answer all the questions of this group. [1 x 20 = 20]l. The probability that a number selected at random between 100 and 999 (both inclusive) will not containthe digit 7 isll. A class is composed of 2 brothers and 5 other guys. The number of ways all the boys can be seated in around table so thdt two brothers are not seated together is .............'.....f lf . Given the relation R = {(7,2]1,12,3)}.The minimum number of ordered pairs that must be added to this Setso that the enlarged relation becomes reflexive, symmetric and transitive is ...................lV. Considerthe mapping f:X -+ Y. f is a bijection if and only if(a) f(x) = f(y) implies x = y for all x, y (b) range of f is Y(c ) both (a) and (b) are true (d)the co-domain equals to rangeV. Let A and B be two arbitrary events. Then(a) P(A nB) =p141 + P(B) (b) P(AUB) = P(A)+P(B)(c) P(A/B)= P(An B)+P(B) (d) P (Au B) < P(A)+P(B)Vl. The subset of a countable set(a) has to be countable (b) may or may not be countable(c) has to be finite (d) none ofthe aboveVll. Every element of some ring(R,+,*),is such that a *a = a. The ring '(a) is commutative (b) is not commutative(c) may or may not be commutative (d) none of the aboveVlll. The number of subsets of {1,2...n} of odd cardinality is(a) Dependant on the value of n (b) 2n-1if n is odd(. I 2n't if n is even (d) 2*t for any value of nfX. The set {1,2,3, 4, 6,8, 12,24ltogether with GCD as binary operation is not a group because(a) it is not associative (b) identity does not exist(c ) inverse is not unique (d) inverse does not existx. tf the proposition.-P is true, then the truth value of the proposition -Pv(P +Q) is(a)trire (b) multi-valued ( c ) false (d) cannot be determinedXl. Translate the following statement into symbols using quantifiers, variables and predicate symbols" All men are giants."Xll. Translate the following statement into symbols using quantifiers, variables and predicate symbols'There is a student who likes mathematics but not history."xlll. Determine the truth or falsity of the following sentence where universe is the set of integers3x, [{x2 > 10} n x is even}]XlV. Determine the truth or falsity of the following sentence where universe is the set of integers:Vx, {3Y,[x2 = Y]]Page 7. of 2

